#### Article 71

Prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter a shall be implemented through:
a. implementation of policies, programs, and activities for prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area;  
b. provision of education on prevention activities for VAC involving parties in the Regency Area;  
c. enhancement of participation of the Community, Business Sector, media, and Children in prevention of VAC in the Regency Area; andd. strengthening of cooperation to realize CFC, child-friendly sub-districts, and child-friendly villages/urban villages.

#### Article 72

1. Prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter a shall be implemented in accordance with standards and procedures.  
2. Standards for prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
3. Procedures for prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1) shall consist of:a. development and strengthening of institutional framework for prevention of VAC;  
b. policy advocacy and assistance or technical guidance on implementation of policies, programs, and activities for prevention of VAC in the Regency Area;  
andc. coordination and synchronization of prevention of VAC in the Regency Area.

#### Article 73

1. Prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter a shall be measured using criteria.  
2. Criteria for Prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1) shall consist of:a. number of Regional Apparatus implementing prevention of VAC;  
b. percentage of human resources of Regional Apparatus trained on prevention of VAC;  
c. number of CSOs, communities, Business Sector, media, and Children's Forums participating in prevention of VAC;  
andd. increase in the value of the Special Protection of Children cluster in CFC.

#### Article 74

Provision of services for CNSP requiring coordination in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter b shall be implemented through:
a. receipt of reports or outreach to CNSP;  
b. provision of information about the rights of CNSP;  
c. facilitating the provision of health services;  
d. facilitating the provision of psychological strengthening services;  
e. facilitating the provision of psychosocial services, Social Rehabilitation, social empowerment, and Social Reintegration;  
f. provision of legal services;  
g. identifying temporary shelter needs; h. facilitating the needs of Victims with disabilities; andi. cooperating on the fulfillment of CNSP rights with other institutions.

#### Article 75

1. Provision of services for CNSP requiring coordination in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter b shall be implemented in accordance with standards and procedures.  
2. Standards for provision of services for CNSP as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be the standards for Child Protection services.  
3. Procedures for provision of services for CNSP as referred to in paragraph (1) shall consist of:a. provision of community complaint services for CNSP in the Regency Area including:
1. establishment of UPTD PPA in the Regency Area;  
2. implementation of UPTD PPA services; and
3. provision and strengthening of human resources of service providers through training and certification of CNSP protection services.  b. coordination and synchronization of implementation of assistance to CNSP in the Regency Area including:
1. coordination …
1. cross-Regional Apparatus coordination for implementation of provision of services for CNSP;  
2. policy development and implementation of an integrated CNSP handling system across related Regional Apparatus;  
3. guidance to the Regency Area in handling CNSP; and
4. data collection, monitoring, and evaluation of CNSP case services.

#### Article 76

1. Achievement of provision of services for CNSP requiring coordination in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter b shall be measured using criteria.  
2. Criteria for achievement of provision of services for CNSP as referred to in paragraph (1) shall include:a. number of CNSP services; andb. percentage of CNSP complaints receiving comprehensive services appropriate to the needs of victims.

#### Article 77

Strengthening and development of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter c shall be implemented through:
a. capacity building of institutional resources of service provider institutions for handling CNSP in the Regency Area;  
b. provision of assistance for special needs of CNSP in the Regency Area;  
c. provision of communication, information, and education on protection of CNSP in the Regency Area;  
d. strengthening of networks among service provider institutions for protection of CNSP in the Regency Area;  
e. facilitation of implementation of standardization of service provider institutions for protection of CNSP in the Regency Area; andf. development of service provider institutions for protection of CNSP in the Regency Area.

#### Article 78

1. Strengthening and development of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter c shall be implemented in accordance with standards and procedures.  
2. Standards for strengthening and development of service provider institutions as referred to in paragraph (1) shall include standards for child-friendly Special Protection institutions.  
3. Procedures for strengthening and development of service provider institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1) shall include:a. coordination and synchronization of provision of service facilities and infrastructure for CNSP in the Regency Area;  
b. capacity building …b. capacity building of human resources of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area; andc. strengthening of networks among Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area.

#### Article 79

1. Achievement of strengthening and development of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter c shall be measured using criteria.  
2. Criteria for achievement of strengthening and development of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP as referred to in paragraph (1) shall include:a. percentage of human resources of service providers trained and receiving certificates in protection and handling of CNSP;  
b. percentage of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area having service facilities and infrastructure in accordance with standards;  
c. percentage of CNSP receiving assistance for special needs; andd. percentage of Service Provider Institutions for CNSP in the Regency Area standardized as child-friendly.

#### Article 80

Further provisions regarding the implementation of Special Protection of Children in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 60 through Article 78, shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

## Part Seven Child-Friendly Regency

#### Article 81

1. The Regency Regional Government shall implement CFC in the Regency Area.  
2. Implementation of CFC in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through integration of policies, programs, and activities for development of the Central Government and Regency Regional Government.  
3. Further provisions regarding the Implementation of CFC as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a separate Regional Regulation.

# CHAPTER V IMPROVEMENT OF FAMILY QUALITY

## Part One General

#### Article 82 (1) The Regency Regional Government shall have the authority to implement Improvement of Family Quality in the Regency Area.  

2. Implementation of Improvement of Family Quality in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in order to support the development of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the Regency Area.  
3. Implementation of Improvement of Family Quality in the Regency Area as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out by the Regency Regional Apparatus implementing governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
